<title>ITALY: Chase Nominees buys stakes in Italy's Credito, IMI.</title>
<headline>Chase Nominees buys stakes in Italy's Credito, IMI.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. fund Chase Nominees Ltd has acquired a 2.06 percent stake in Italian bank Credito Italiano and has also raised its stake in Italian investment bank IMI, said stock market watchdog body Consob.</p>
<p>In a statement, Consob said that Chase Nominees had raised its stake in IMI to 3.06 percent from 2.03 percent, and also had increased its holding in publishing group Mondadori to 3.4 percent from 2.3 percent.</p>
<p>Italian financial daily Il Sole 24 Ore reported on Thursday that U.S. fund group Fidelity had bought a 3.1 percent stake in Credito.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
